{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]I know that my [G]Re[D]deem[E7]er [A]lives;
[D]What comfort [G]this [D]sweet [Em]sen[D]tence [A]gives!
[D]He lives, [A7]He [D]lives, who [G]once [A7]was__[D]__ [A]dead;
[D]He [G]lives, my [D]ever liv__[A7]__ing [D]head.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]He lives to bless [G]me [D]with [E7]His [A]love,
[D]He lives to [G]plead [D]for [Em]me [D]a[A]bove.
[D]He lives [A7]my [D]hungry [G]soul [A7]to__[D]__ [A]feed,
[D]He [G]lives to [D]help in time__[A7]__ of [D]need.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]He lives trium[G]phant [D]from [E7]the [A]grave,
[D]He lives e[G]ter[D]nal[Em]ly [D]to [A]save,
[D]He lives [A7]all [D]glorious [G]in [A7]the__[D]__ [A]sky,
[D]He [G]lives ex[D]alted there__[A7]__ on [D]high.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]He lives to grant [G]me [D]rich [E7]sup[A]ply,
[D]He lives to [G]guide [D]me [Em]with [D]His [A]eye,
[D]He lives [A7]to [D]comfort [G]me [A7]when__[D]__ [A]faint,
[D]He [G]lives to [D]hear my soul’s__[A7]__ com[D]plaint.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]He lives to si[G]lence [D]all [E7]my [A]fears,
[D]He lives to [G]wipe [D]a[Em]way [D]my [A]tears
[D]He lives [A7]to [D]calm my [G]trou[A7]bled__[D]__ [A]heart,
[D]He [G]lives all [D]blessings to__[A7]__ im[D]part.
{end_of_verse}
